                        ],
                        "form": "afgeschuimd"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39a97b54-6875-368a-855d-576cbb710236",
                        "entry_id": "8f9e77cc-b690-3b0d-bf35-c0cb4b1ce0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to remove foam"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b3c9ec5-32dc-4da9-9977-f864634d1057",
                                "sense_id": "39a97b54-6875-368a-855d-576cbb710236",
                                "text": "Gedurende het afschuimen moet de oplossing steeds kokende gehouden worden, waardoor de digtheid van het vocht toeneemt, en het schuim gemakkelijker naar boven stijgt; men zorgt daarbij echter, dat door het te sterk koken, het schuim niet over den rand des ketels loopt.",
                                "translation": "During the removal of foam the solution should be continuously kept boiling, which causes the density of the fluid to increase, and the foam will rise up more easily; precaution should be taken however, that by boiling at a too high temperature or pressure the foam doesn't run over the rim of the rettle.",
                                "english": "During the removal of foam the solution should be continuously kept boiling, which causes the density of the fluid to increase, and the foam will rise up more easily; precaution should be taken however, that by boiling at a too high temperature or pressure the foam doesn't run over the rim of the rettle."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5c6888d-0259-3feb-8012-5dd95829ecf1",
                        "entry_id": "8f9e77cc-b690-3b0d-bf35-c0cb4b1ce0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to remove impurities (from)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa4b5c0d-0bb7-40ed-85c2-0eb594fad2ec",
                                "sense_id": "d5c6888d-0259-3feb-8012-5dd95829ecf1",
                                "text": "1853, P. F. Klijnsma, \"Het ijzer. Zijne smelting en bewerking\", in Algemeen handboek van kunsten en wetenschappen. Nijverheid, vol. 8, in, Volks-bibliotheek, Weijtingh & Brave, 17.\nTusschen de kruin van den dam en het uiteinde der ijzeren plaat, die het onderste gedeelte van het gewelf der werkplaats draagt, bevindt zich het schepgat, waardoor men in den kroes zien, en het noodige werk onder in den oven verrigten kan, zooals het afschuimen van de overtollige vreemde stoffen van het ijzer en het scheppen hiervan met lepels tot het gieten van verschillende voorwerpen in vormen, enz.",
                                "translation": "(please add an English translation of this quotation)",
                                "english": "(please add an English translation of this quotation)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f10f8724-73a0-3217-8e84-5a2e111e789d",
                        "entry_id": "8f9e77cc-b690-3b0d-bf35-c0cb4b1ce0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to plunder, to rob"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aba5886d-4be3-4be6-82ed-d697e84496dd",
                                "sense_id": "f10f8724-73a0-3217-8e84-5a2e111e789d",
                                "text": "1838, Adriaan van der Hoop, Junior, De Renegaat. Een berymd verhaal, Elix & co., 80-81.\nOn ne se souvient plus des promesses, quand les périls sont passés, zegt het fransche spreekwoord: het was het motto, dat de Algerijnen immer schreven op het teboekstellen hunner verdragen; want by iedere verademing, na eene ontfangene tuchtiging, schuimden die Korsaren den Oceaan roofgieriger af dan ooit.",
                                "translation": "One no longer follows through on promises, when the threats have passed, says the French proverb: it was the motto that the Algerians always wrote on the codifications of their treaties; for during every respite, after a received punitive expedition, those Corsairs plundered the ocean more rapaciously than ever.",
                                "english": "One no longer follows through on promises, when the threats have passed, says the French proverb: it was the motto that the Algerians always wrote on the codifications of their treaties; for during every respite, after a received punitive expedition, those Corsairs plundered the ocean more rapaciously than ever."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf058c86-180e-4c52-88e4-45cda0b8b756",
                                "sense_id": "f10f8724-73a0-3217-8e84-5a2e111e789d",
                                "text": "Ze schuimden de straten af, kwamen vooral in het donker uit hun schuilplaatsen tevoorschijn.",
                                "translation": "They plundered the streets, and came out of their hiding places mostly under the cover of darkness.",
                                "english": "They plundered the streets, and came out of their hiding places mostly under the cover of darkness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d67fc60e-e2fa-499d-8f77-4cc975f6460f",
                                "sense_id": "f10f8724-73a0-3217-8e84-5a2e111e789d",
                                "text": "Roversbendes en zakkenrollers schuimden de straten af en moorden waren aan de orde van de dag.",
                                "translation": "Gangs of robbers, and pickpockets, plundered the streets and murders were a daily occurrence.",
                                "english": "Gangs of robbers, and pickpockets, plundered the streets and murders were a daily occurrence."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6c640d26-3a8f-3ee6-80db-1e0f075a66cc",
                        "entry_id": "8f9e77cc-b690-3b0d-bf35-c0cb4b1ce0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to rummage, to scour"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdfb21db-6169-4194-8306-41540aa20956",
                                "sense_id": "6c640d26-3a8f-3ee6-80db-1e0f075a66cc",
                                "text": "2002, Jan Frans Verbruggen & Rolf Falter, 1302: Opstand in Vlaanderen, Lannoo, 121.\nRoofridders schuimden de wegen af om handelaars te plunderen met het motief dat ze voor de andere partij werkten.",
                                "translation": "Robber barons scoured the roads to plunder merchants under the motive that they worked for the other party.",
                                "english": "Robber barons scoured the roads to plunder merchants under the motive that they worked for the other party."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "825060eb-2d3a-4837-9225-76bf65f43e16",
                                "sense_id": "6c640d26-3a8f-3ee6-80db-1e0f075a66cc",
                                "text": "De mannen van het gerecht schuimden de tentoonstellingsruimten af en bepotelden zowat alles, op zoek naar vingerafdrukken van de onverlaat die de magistraat had mishandeld — wat zei hij, opengesneden was een juistere uitdrukking — en voor bijna dood had achtergelaten.",
                                "translation": "The men from law enforcement scoured the exposition rooms and fingered nearly everything, in search of finger prints from the miscreant who abused the magistrate — what did he say, cut open was a more correct expression — and had left her behind near dead.",
                                "english": "The men from law enforcement scoured the exposition rooms and fingered nearly everything, in search of finger prints from the miscreant who abused the magistrate — what did he say, cut open was a more correct expression — and had left her behind near dead."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
